From: Chad Monroe <chad.monroe@adtran.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] spi: gpio: drive the clock to its idle level at setup

spi-gpio requests SCK as GPIOD_OUT_LOW and moves it to the CPOL idle
level only inside chipselect(), so a mode 3 device sees SCLK low until
its first transfer. A device held in reset across the boot can sample
SCLK when the reset releases: the Si32184 SLIC on the SDG-8716v ignores
its bus after a reset edge that saw SCLK low, and the first transfer
(the probe that follows the release) comes too late. Drive SCK to the
idle level of the device's mode in setup(), so the line rests at the
right level from the moment the device exists. chipselect() keeps
setting it per transfer, so a bus shared by devices of different
polarity behaves as before.
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-gpio.c
@@ -235,6 +235,14 @@ static int spi_gpio_setup(struct spi_dev
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Park the clock at its idle level now, not at the first chip select:
+	 * a device held in reset across the boot can sample SCLK when its
+	 * reset releases, long before the first transfer (the Si32184 SLIC
+	 * ignores its bus after a reset edge that saw SCLK low).
+	 */
+	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(spi_gpio->sck, !!(spi->mode & SPI_CPOL));
+
 	return spi_bitbang_setup(spi);
 }
 
